<section class="section-muted deferred-section">
  <div class="page-shell px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[940px]">
      <h2 class="text-center text-[1.45rem] font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-12 space-y-5">
        <article class="rounded-[8px] border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm hover:bg-slate-100">
          <button type="button" class="faq-toggle flex w-full items-center justify-between px-8 py-6 text-left">
            <span class="text-[1rem] font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Why is this image especially useful for Catholic websites or church content?</span>
            <svg class="faq-icon h-6 w-6 text-slate-400 transition-transform" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer hidden px-8 pb-6 text-[14px] leading-6 text-slate-600">It visually represents core Catholic doctrine — the Sacred Heart as a symbol of divine love, sacrifice, and mercy. Its dramatic imagery instantly communicates spiritual depth and devotion, making it ideal for sermons, devotionals, or worship pages.</div>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-[8px] border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm hover:bg-slate-100">
          <button type="button" class="faq-toggle flex w-full items-center justify-between px-8 py-6 text-left">
            <span class="text-[1rem] font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Can this image be used for social media campaigns focused on faith?</span>
            <svg class="faq-icon h-6 w-6 text-slate-400 transition-transform" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer hidden px-8 pb-6 text-[14px] leading-6 text-slate-600">Absolutely. The strong emotional symbolism and recognizable iconography make it highly effective for social media graphics, especially for posts about mercy, prayer, or spiritual renewal, resonating with followers seeking spiritual connection.</div>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-[8px] border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm hover:bg-slate-100">
          <button type="button" class="faq-toggle flex w-full items-center justify-between px-8 py-6 text-left">
            <span class="text-[1rem] font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Is this image suitable for educational materials about religion?</span>
            <svg class="faq-icon h-6 w-6 text-slate-400 transition-transform" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer hidden px-8 pb-6 text-[14px] leading-6 text-slate-600">Yes. Its clear visual storytelling helps explain complex theological concepts like sacrifice and divine love, making it a powerful tool for religious education, youth groups, or classroom presentations.</div>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-[8px] border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm hover:bg-slate-100">
          <button type="button" class="faq-toggle flex w-full items-center justify-between px-8 py-6 text-left">
            <span class="text-[1rem] font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">What makes this image stand out for spiritual content creators?</span>
            <svg class="faq-icon h-6 w-6 text-slate-400 transition-transform" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer hidden px-8 pb-6 text-[14px] leading-6 text-slate-600">The combination of anatomical detail, thorn crown, flame, and cross creates a layered, emotionally charged image that conveys both suffering and divine love — a rare and impactful visual for spiritual content.</div>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-[8px] border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm hover:bg-slate-100">
          <button type="button" class="faq-toggle flex w-full items-center justify-between px-8 py-6 text-left">
            <span class="text-[1rem] font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Can this image be used in reaction or lifestyle content about faith?</span>
            <svg class="faq-icon h-6 w-6 text-slate-400 transition-transform" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer hidden px-8 pb-6 text-[14px] leading-6 text-slate-600">Yes. Its dramatic and emotive style works well in reaction posts, devotional blogs, or lifestyle content focused on spiritual growth, making it a compelling visual anchor for audiences seeking meaning and connection.</div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


